# Nakharax Protocol Rule

## Architecture & Isolation
- **Strict Isolation:** NakharaX Protocol is strictly Layer-1 DeAI Compute Marketplace & Sovereign OS. Never mix external projects (XpFirm / MT5 Prop Firm) into this repo.
- Check `packages/sdk` first for reusable business logic before implementing in apps.
- Use workspace aliases only (e.g. `@nakharax/sdk`, `@nakharax/contracts`), never cross-package relative imports.
- Use `pnpm` exclusively for workspace dependencies and scripts (`pnpm dev:web`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm reality:check`).

## Frontend (`apps/os-dashboard/`)
- Default to React Server Components; add `"use client"` only when hooks/browser APIs are required.
- Use Tailwind CSS and keep dark, cyberpunk/futuristic styling as default.
- Use `next/image` for UI images when possible.
- State management with Zustand; Web3 interactions via Viem.

## Integration and Reliability
- If node/validator access is unavailable, use `pnpm mock-rpc` (`services/core/ops/deploy/mock-rpc/server.js`) to unblock UI development.
- Handle RPC and transaction failures gracefully with clear user-facing feedback.
- Verify ground truth with `pnpm reality:check` (100% Truth Score).

## Rust & Python Core Context (`services/core/`)
- When tasks mention Core or Node, treat it as the Rust/Python consensus and DeAI worker implementation.
- Favor memory safety, predictable behavior, and performance-minded changes.

## Working Style
- Keep changes concise and practical; include TypeScript interfaces for new components.
- After edits, verify imports and workspace references remain valid.
